  "title": "Equidistribution of Integer Multiples",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $c > 0$ and let $A$ be a set of $n$ distinct integers. Does there exist $\\theta$ such that no interval of length $\\frac{1}{n}$ in $\\mathbb{R}/\\mathbb{Z}$ contains more than $n^c$ of the numbers $\\theta a \\pmod 1$, for $a \\in A$?",
